```
$ jci-audit prune -h
Stale-ignore detector for advisory ignores that no longer fire

Usage: jci-audit prune [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --check       Fail (non-zero) when a stale ignore is found. For CI
  -v, --verbose...  Increase logging verbosity
  -q, --quiet...    Decrease logging verbosity
  -h, --help        Print help (see more with '--help')

$ jci-audit prune --help
Stale-ignore detector for advisory ignores that no longer fire.

Runs audit/deny against the naked advisory-db (no local ignores applied) to find configured ignores that no longer fire.

Usage: jci-audit prune [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --check
          Fail (non-zero) when a stale ignore is found. For CI

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase logging verbosity

  -q, --quiet...
          Decrease logging verbosity

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

```
